sections.context:
The worktree infrastructure from P02 already supports multiple concurrent worktrees (worker-1, worker-2, worker-3). Phase 3 adds the concurrency controller.

**Resource monitoring:** Use PowerShell's Get-Counter or WMI to read CPU and memory. Apply the same threshold logic as the server-side scaling policy (W10):
- Start another session when: CPU < 60%, memory < 80%, queue has work
- Don't start new sessions when: CPU > 80% or memory > 80%
- Maximum sessions: configurable, default 3

**Concurrency model:** Each CC session runs in a PowerShell job or background process.
```powershell
$jobs = @{}
while ($true) {
    # Clean up completed jobs and their worktrees
    foreach ($id in @($jobs.Keys)) {
        if ($jobs[$id].Job.State -ne 'Running') {
            Invoke-PostTaskHandler $jobs[$id].Issue $jobs[$id].Job
            Remove-AgentWorktree $jobs[$id].WorktreePath
            $jobs.Remove($id)
        }
    }
    # Check if we can start more
    if ($jobs.Count -lt $maxSessions -and (Test-ResourceHeadroom)) {
        $issue = Get-NextClaimableIssue
        if ($issue) {
            $slot = Get-AvailableWorkerSlot
            $worktree = New-AgentWorktree -Slot $slot -Branch "fix/$($issue.Number)"
            $job = Start-Job { Invoke-CCSession $using:issue $using:worktree }
            $jobs[$slot] = @{Job=$job; Issue=$issue; WorktreePath=$worktree}
        }
    }
    Start-Sleep 30
}
```

Config additions to pc-agent.yaml:
```yaml
concurrency:
  max_sessions: 3
  cpu_ceiling: 80
  memory_ceiling: 80
```
